CODEBASE REVIEW
• Scan the entire existing codebase before making any changes.
• Reuse existing components wherever possible to avoid duplication.

DOCUMENTATION & COMMENTING
• Add clear inline comments for every change, explaining purpose, logic, and dependencies.
• Create or update external design documentation detailing changes, rationale, and integration approach.

TESTING AND VERIFICATION
• Run the project after modifications to ensure there are no errors.
• Develop detailed test cases covering at least 90% of the modified code.
• Confirm that all tests pass before marking the update as complete.

DATA HANDLING & API PREPARATION
• Do not hardcode static data within component files.
• Fetch data via dedicated service files that can later be replaced with real API calls (use dummy data in the stubbed methods for now).

COMPONENT USAGE & STRUCTURE
• Leverage ShadCN UI components instead of creating custom ones when possible.
• Break the implementation into small, self‑contained components, each with a single responsibility.
• Organize components into clearly labeled folders for ease of maintenance.

USER EXPERIENCE (UX) CONSIDERATIONS
• Prioritize mobile responsiveness while maintaining a high‑quality desktop experience.
• Design a simple, intuitive UI for school teachers and students with limited technical skills.
• Keep navigation minimal and straightforward.

PLANNING & APPROVAL
• Draft a comprehensive design document outlining changes, architecture decisions, and integration points.
• Start coding only after the design document has been reviewed and approved.

ERROR HANDLING
• Do not suppress errors—address and fix them immediately.
• Adopt a fail‑fast approach: stop and resolve issues as soon as they occur.

ADDITIONAL REMINDERS
• Do not commit code changes directly to Git.
• When available, use npx instead of npm.
• Ensure the UI remains simple and intuitive for non‑technical users.

MOST IMPORTANT:
Whenever you create any modules, provide separate components, views, and everything else for each user type (STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER, ADMIN).